    {
      "id": "be-s9-exponential-smoothing-c3",
      "heading": "Worked question: α = 0.3",
      "explanation_md": "Sales from 2020 to 2024 are 100, 120, 110, 130 and 140. Take the **first actual as the first forecast**: F2021 = 100.\n\n| Year | Actual | Working | Forecast |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2021 | 120 | first actual | 100.00 |\n| 2022 | 110 | 0.3 x 120 + 0.7 x 100 = 36 + 70 | 106.00 |\n| 2023 | 130 | 0.3 x 110 + 0.7 x 106 = 33 + 74.2 | 107.20 |\n| 2024 | 140 | 0.3 x 130 + 0.7 x 107.2 = 39 + 75.04 | 114.04 |\n| 2025 | | 0.3 x 140 + 0.7 x 114.04 = 42 + 79.828 | **121.83** |",
      "example_ids": [
        "be-ex-smoothing-alpha-03"
      ],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Start with F = the first actual, then apply F(t+1) = 0.3Y(t) + 0.7F(t) year by year: F2025 = 121.83.",
      "clarification": null,
      "check_questions": [
