    {
      "id": "be-s9-exponential-smoothing-q-fdb0690b",
      "type": "long",
      "stem": "For 2017 to 2025 sales of 80, 85, 90, 100, 120, 110, 130, 140 and 150, forecast 2026 by a 3-year moving average and by exponential smoothing with α = 0.1, and use RMSE to choose the better model.",
      "options": [],
      "answer": "",
      "accept": [],
      "explanation": "",
      "model_answer_md": "**3-year moving average:** 2026 = (130 + 140 + 150) / 3 = **140**, RMSE about **20.07** over 2020 to 2025.\n\n**Exponential smoothing, α = 0.1**, starting from the first actual (80) as the first forecast: forecasts 80.5, 81.45, 83.31, 86.97, 89.28, 93.35 and 98.01 for 2019 to 2025, and about **103.21** for 2026. Over the same six years (2020 to 2025) its RMSE is about **38.21**.\n\nThe moving average has the **lower RMSE**, so it is the preferable model for this data: with α = 0.1, smoothing lags behind sales that keep rising.",
